module lawd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.louisiana.{ frcp6-louisiana }

// The Western District of Louisiana's own civil periods, computed under
// the federal rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). The motion
// briefing periods are the default rule only: for a contested motion the
// clerk ordinarily issues a Notice of Motion Setting with the briefing
// deadlines, and a judge may order other instructions (LR 7.4); the
// periods below apply when neither issues. A judge may grant leave to
// exceed the memorandum page limits in an extraordinary case, and a
// memorandum over 10 pages needs tables of contents and authorities (LR
// 7.1); LR 7.8 states the same limits for briefs. Objections to an item
// of costs "within seven days" (LR 54.4) state no starting event, so they
// stay in this note; review of the clerk's taxation within seven days (LR
// 54.5) is FRCP 54(d)(1)'s period and belongs to lit/frcp. The court's
// own grounds for dismissal for lack of prosecution (no service within 90
// days of filing, no responsive pleading or default within 60 days of
// service, six months without proceedings, a returned address left
// uncorrected for 30 days: LR 41.3) are court actions, so they stay in
// this note. Attorney admission and discipline (LR 83.2) are not encoded.
// The earlier W.D. La. outline's FRCP flow and its decisions (Twombly,
// Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson, Matsushita, Frow v. De La Vega) are FRCP
// authority and belong to lit/frcp; they are removed here: no reporter
// text is vendored.
/// A memorandum in support of or in opposition to a motion: at most 25
/// pages, exclusive of a table of contents or table of authorities
/// (W.D. La. LR 7.1).
limit memorandum { pages <= 25 cite "W.D. La. LR 7.1" } cite "W.D. La. LR 7.1"
/// A reply memorandum: at most 10 pages (W.D. La. LR 7.1).
limit reply-memorandum { pages <= 10 cite "W.D. La. LR 7.1" } cite "W.D. La. LR 7.1"

/// A document bearing several signatures is served electronically
/// (W.D. La. LR 5.7.08).
event MultiSignatureDocumentServed()
/// A motion is filed (W.D. La. LR 7.4).
event MotionFiled() paper memorandum
/// A memorandum in opposition to a motion is filed (W.D. La. LR 7.4).
event OppositionFiled() paper memorandum
/// A reply memorandum is filed (W.D. La. LR 7.4).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-memorandum
/// The scheduling order's deadline for close of discovery passes
/// (W.D. La. LR 16.3.1).
event DiscoveryCloseDeadline()
/// Notice of a proposed dismissal for failure to prosecute is mailed to
/// the plaintiff (W.D. La. LR 41.3).
event ProsecutionNoticeMailed()
/// An order dismissing the action for failure to prosecute is entered
/// (W.D. La. LR 41.3).
event ProsecutionDismissalOrdered()
/// The date on which the jury trial is scheduled (W.D. La. LR 51.1).
event JuryTrialScheduled()
/// The prevailing party receives notice of entry of judgment
/// (W.D. La. LR 54.3).
event JudgmentEntryNoticed()
/// The clerk enters default (W.D. La. LR 55.1).
event DefaultEntered()
/// The civil case is finally disposed of (W.D. La. LR 79.3).
event FinalDisposition()

/// W.D. La. LR 5.7.08: a non-filing signatory or party who disputes the
/// authenticity of an electronically filed document with several
/// signatures, or of the signatures, files an objection within 14 days
/// from service of the document.
deadline signature-objection-period: 14.days after MultiSignatureDocumentServed() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 5.7.08"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 7.4: if no Notice of Motion Setting issues and the judge
/// orders no briefing instructions, a memorandum in opposition may be
/// filed within 14 days after the motion is filed.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 7.4"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 7.4: under the same default rule, a reply memorandum may
/// be filed within seven days after the opposition is filed.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after OppositionFiled() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 7.4"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 16.3.1: within 60 days after the deadline for close of
/// discovery (and before the initial Rule 26(f) conference), counsel
/// discuss with their clients and opposing counsel the appropriateness and
/// timing of alternative dispute resolution.
deadline adr-conference-period: 60.days after DiscoveryCloseDeadline() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 16.3.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 41.3: before a dismissal for failure to prosecute, the
/// plaintiff has 30 calendar days from mailing of the notice to file
/// evidence of good cause; with no response in time the clerk may dismiss.
deadline prosecution-good-cause-period: 30.days after ProsecutionNoticeMailed() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 41.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 41.3: a dismissal for failure to prosecute is without
/// prejudice, and the order allows reinstatement within 30 days for good
/// cause shown.
deadline reinstatement-period: 30.days after ProsecutionDismissalOrdered() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 41.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 51.1: unless the court orders otherwise, the joint and
/// separate proposed jury instructions are filed, with a copy to the
/// trial judge, at least seven days in advance of the date on which the
/// jury trial is scheduled.
deadline jury-instructions-period: 7.days before JuryTrialScheduled() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 51.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 54.3: within 30 days after receiving notice of entry of
/// judgment, unless otherwise ordered, the prevailing party serves and
/// files a Bill of Costs with a supporting memorandum; without the
/// memorandum the clerk may deny costs.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntryNoticed() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 54.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 55.1: a judgment of default is not entered until 14
/// calendar days after entry of default; this is the earliest date, not a
/// last day.
deadline default-judgment-waiting-period: 14.days after DefaultEntered() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 55.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. La. LR 79.3: exhibits in civil cases in the clerk's custody are
/// removed within 30 days of the final disposition of the case, or may be
/// destroyed or otherwise disposed of by the clerk.
deadline exhibit-removal-period: 30.days after FinalDisposition() counted_by frcp6-louisiana cite "W.D. La. LR 79.3"
{
  forum frcp
}
